\DOC genvar_index_goal

\TYPE {genvar_index_goal : goal -> int}

\SYNOPSIS
Returns a starting number for fresh variables named like those of genvars for
a goal.

\DESCRIBE
The call {genvar_index_goal (asl,w)} returns the {genvar_index} of all the terms
of the goal: its conclusion {w} and the conclusions and hypotheses of its
assumptions {asl}. So the variables {mk_genvar(n,ty)}, {mk_genvar(n + 1,ty)},
... for that number {n} are fresh for everything in the goal.

\FAILURE
Fails only in the absurd case noted under {genvar_index}.

\USES
Tactics that need fresh variables for a goal.

\SEEALSO
genvar, genvar_index, genvars, mk_genvar.

\ENDDOC
